{"id": "mitre-h01", "question": "Which piece of grid-attacking malware was caught before its scheduled run date in April 2022, so it never caused any damage?", "reference": "Industroyer2 (S1072).", "relevant": [{"path": "software/S1072_industroyer2.md", "evidence": "discovered before deploying, resulting in no impact"}], "answerable": true, "tags": ["base", "has-variants", "hard", "software", "near-duplicate", "ics"], "notes": "Decoys: Industroyer (S0604, the 2016 grid attack) and C0034 (the October 2022 Ukraine power attack, which caused real disruption). Both share names and dates with the answer. Context (not required in an answer): Compiled 23 March 2022 and set to run on 8 April 2022, but discovered before deployment, so it had no impact."}
