{"id": "mitre-vh01", "question": "Several of Cozy Bear's malware families leaned on Twitter as a backup command channel. Which one was only in use from 2013 to 2015, and how does ATT&CK classify its Twitter use differently from CozyCar's?", "reference": "OnionDuke (S0052). ATT&CK classes its Twitter backup C2 as T1102.003 Web Service: One-Way Communication, while CozyCar's Twitter backup channel is T1102.002 Web Service: Bidirectional Communication.", "relevant": [{"path": "software/S0052_onionduke.md", "evidence": "OnionDuke uses Twitter as a backup C2"}, {"path": "software/S0046_cozycar.md", "evidence": "CozyCar uses Twitter as a backup C2 channel"}], "answerable": true, "tags": ["base", "has-variants", "very-hard", "software", "alias", "multi-hop", "comparison", "enterprise"], "notes": "Four steps: resolve the Cozy Bear alias to APT29, pick out OnionDuke by its dates from APT29's Twitter users (MiniDuke 2010-2015, CozyCar 2010-2015), then compare two sub-techniques across two files."}
