{"id": "mitre-u17", "question": "To stop MFA-fatigue attacks, what is the maximum number of push prompts per user per hour that ATT&CK recommends allowing?", "reference": "The documents don't say. ATT&CK advises limiting how many MFA request prompts can be sent to a user in a period of time, but gives no specific number.", "answerable": false, "tags": ["unanswerable", "mitigation", "enterprise", "base", "number"], "notes": "Tempting because M1032 and T1621 explicitly recommend 'limits upon the maximum number of 2FA/MFA request prompts'. Verified: no numeric limit, rate or time window appears near any MFA prompt/push/request mention in M1032, M1036, M1017, T1621 or elsewhere in the corpus."}
{"id": "mitre-u18", "question": "Roughly how many organizations had their SharePoint servers compromised during the July 2025 ToolShell exploitation wave?", "reference": "The documents don't say. ATT&CK's SharePoint ToolShell Exploitation campaign (C0058) covers the CVEs, the actors involved (Storm-2603, Threat Group-3390, ZIRCONIUM), the targeted regions and sectors and the techniques used, but gives no victim count.", "answerable": false, "tags": ["unanswerable", "campaign", "enterprise", "base", "number", "real-incident"], "notes": "Tempting because C0058 and about 40 technique/software files describe ToolShell in detail and public reporting gives victim counts in the hundreds. Verified: no count of organizations, servers or victims appears in any line mentioning ToolShell."}
